      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aliso_Viejo%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was incorporated July 1, 2001, becoming Orange County's 34th city and the only one incorporated since 2000.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aliso_Viejo%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original 6,600-acre Aliso Viejo was part of the 26,000-acre Moulton Ranch, once owned by the Moulton family after 1890s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aliso_Viejo%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 2,600 acres set aside for the Aliso and Wood Canyons Wilderness Park preserve the region's native flora and offer hiking trails.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aliso_Viejo%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
